# Nothing in the build context except the Dockerfile's three COPY targets.
#
# WHY, even though it is already true: the Dockerfile COPYs three files, and
# BuildKit only transfers what a COPY names, so a build here moves 110 bytes
# of context [measured: "transferring context: 2B" and "108B"].
# The classic builder does not do that - it tars the whole directory, which
# runs to gigabytes once a mod-tools copy sits inside it. This file makes the
# image's independence from the tools a property of the repository rather
# than a property of which builder happens to run.
*

!entrypoint.sh
!with-display.sh
!xorg-headless.conf
